<GuideLayout 
  title="Seamless vs Cut-and-Sew: Which is Right for Your Brand?"
  description="Compare the two dominant manufacturing technologies in activewear to determine the best fit for your brand's aesthetic and performance goals."
  publishDate="June 26, 2026"
>
  <p>The choice between seamless knitting and traditional cut-and-sew manufacturing defines your product's fit, feel, and price point. As a multi-disciplinary factory, Fitclo specializes in both, helping our clients navigate this critical decision.</p>

  <h2>1. The Seamless Advantage</h2>
  <p>Seamless technology uses circular knitting machines to create a garment as a single tube. This eliminates side seams, reducing friction and providing a 'second-skin' feel. It's ideal for high-compression yoga wear and intricately mapped ventilation zones.</p>

  <h2>2. The Cut-and-Sew Versatility</h2>
  <p>Traditional cut-and-sew allows for far greater creative freedom. Since pieces are cut from fabric rolls, you can combine different materials (like mesh panels with interlock fabric) and create complex color-blocking patterns that are impossible with seamless machines.</p>

</GuideLayout>
